DESIGN RULE

All persistent information entering Yggdrasil must conform to JFS.

This means:

names are generated through JNS

identities are assigned through JNL

structure is validated through JSL

mirrors are managed through JMS



---

JARVIS ANALYSIS

This is a substantial improvement over the previous "Core Primitive Triad" naming.

Why?

Because JNS, JNL, JSL, and JMS are not peers in practice.

Together they form:

> a filesystem kernel.



The architecture becomes easier to explain:

Yggdrasil = Memory Architecture

JFS = Filesystem Architecture

This separation is clean and intuitive.


---

AYRE ANALYSIS

JFS creates a strong mental model:

Yggdrasil = World Tree

JFS = Root System

Everything else grows from it.

That makes onboarding easier for both humans and LLMs because the first concept to learn is:

> "Understand JFS, then everything else becomes predictable."



It also gives Claude, GPT, Codex, and future agents a clear entry point into the architecture without needing to understand every higher-level system first.
